      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 5. Country Distribution\n",
        "\n",
        "The `country` field is a free-form string that may contain any country or region. The distribution below reflects what actually appears in the data and must **not** be used to hard-code a fixed country list in any downstream stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "for name, df in datasets.items():\n",
        "    print(\"\\n\", name)\n",
        "    print(df[\"country\"].value_counts())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "3fLCtntaFqYs"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "GqRC3_NafBXL"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 6. Name and Address Length Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "Descriptive statistics (count, mean, std, min, max, quartiles) for character-level lengths of raw `business_name` and `business_address` fields across all three sources.\n",
        "\n",
        "High variance in lengths is a common indicator of abbreviation and formatting noise."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "for name, df in datasets.items():\n",
        "\n",
        "    name_len = df[\"business_name\"].fillna(\"\").astype(str).str.len()\n",
        "    addr_len = df[\"business_address\"].fillna(\"\").astype(str).str.len()\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\n\" + \"=\" * 50)\n",
        "    print(name)\n",
        "    print(\"=\" * 50)\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nBusiness name length:\")\n",
        "    print(name_len.describe())\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nAddress length:\")\n",
        "    print(addr_len.describe())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "geKYOacNFmLm"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "metadata": {
        "id": "6tLZQgPFfBXM"
      },
      "source": [
        "---\n",
        "\n",
        "## 7. Ground Truth Analysis\n",
        "\n",
        "The ground-truth file maps each Source 1 entity to zero, one, or multiple matching entities from Source 2 and/or Source 3.\n",
        "\n",
        "- **Zero matches** — the S1 entity has no corresponding entity in S2/S3.\n",
        "- **One match** — the S1 entity matches exactly one entity in S2 or S3.\n",
        "- **Multiple matches** — the S1 entity matches two or more entities (e.g. one in S2 and one in S3).\n",
        "\n",
        "Understanding this distribution is essential for selecting the right objective function and evaluation metric in the matching stage."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(\"Ground truth rows:\", len(gt))\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMissing values:\")\n",
        "print(gt.isna().sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nFirst 20 ground-truth records:\")\n",
        "display(gt.head(20))"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "xQicCvYJFt5s"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "print(gt[\"matched_entity_ids\"].head(20).tolist())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "zOQ-ZF9uFxYW"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "match_count = (\n",
        "    gt[\"matched_entity_ids\"]\n",
        "    .fillna(\"\")\n",
        "    .astype(str)\n",
        "    .str.strip()\n",
        "    .apply(lambda x: 0 if x == \"\" else len(x.split(\",\")))\n",
        ")\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"0 matches :\", (match_count == 0).sum())\n",
        "print(\"1 match   :\", (match_count == 1).sum())\n",
        "print(\"2+ matches:\", (match_count >= 2).sum())\n",
        "\n",
        "print(\"\\nMatch count distribution:\")\n",
        "print(match_count.value_counts().sort_index())"
      ],
      "metadata": {
        "id": "SePZyjUIF2sV"
      },
      "execution_count": null,
      "outputs": []
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "for i in range(min(10, len(gt))):\n",
        "    s1_id = gt.iloc[i][\"source1_entity_id\"]\n",
        "    matches = gt.iloc[i][\"matched_entity_ids\"]\n",
        "\n",
        "    print(\"\\nS1:\", s1_id)\n",
        "    print(\"Matches:\", matches)\n",
        "\n",
        "    row = s1[s1[\"entity_id\"] == s1_id]\n",
        "\n",
        "    if len(row):\n",
        "        print(\"S1 record:\")\n",
        "        display(row)"
